## S3 Configuration and state backup

Save the current running configuration to startup configuration before making the change.
Create an additional backup on the approved TFTP server at 192.0.2.20.
Record the current software version and key operational state with the change record.

Commands:
`copy running-config startup-config`
`copy running-config tftp:`

Example TFTP destination:
`192.0.2.20`

Do not continue if the configuration backup fails.

## S4 Image transfer and MD5 verification

Copy the approved IOS-XE image from the approved TFTP server at 192.0.2.20 to bootflash.
Confirm that the file is present and that sufficient storage remains.
Verify the MD5 checksum of the transferred image against the checksum supplied with the approved change package.

Commands:
`copy tftp: bootflash:`
`dir bootflash:`
`verify /md5 bootflash:<image-name>`

Do not continue if the calculated MD5 checksum does not match the approved checksum.

## S5 Boot variable configuration

Configure the new IOS-XE image as the first boot option.
Keep the currently working image configured as the second boot option so that it remains available for recovery.
Verify the resulting boot configuration before scheduling the reload.

Example:
`boot system flash bootflash:<new-image-name>`
`boot system flash bootflash:<old-image-name>`

Verification:
`show running-config | include boot`

Do not remove the previous working image during the change.